# Shell scripts keep LF on every platform. With core.autocrlf=true a checkout
# writes CRLF here, which leaves a trailing \r on each line; whether that breaks
# the script depends on the bash build's willingness to strip it (Git Bash does,
# WSL bash does not, and a stray \r inside a variable survives into URLs and
# arguments). Pinning LF removes that dependency.
*.sh text eol=lf